The o200k_base tokenizer in src/host/o200k.ts (dist/host/o200k.js) is built from two MIT-licensed sources.

o200k_base.tiktoken, beside this file, is OpenAI's o200k_base vocabulary, unchanged: the file tiktoken loads, from
https://openaipublic.blob.core.windows.net/encodings/o200k_base.tiktoken, sha256
446a9538cb6c348e3516120d7c08b09f57c36495e2acfffe59a5bf8b0cfb1a2d, as pinned in tiktoken at commit
79dc2c0533685b893616c78160b5d9e40876e724 (https://github.com/openai/tiktoken).

The split pattern is tiktoken's o200k_base pattern as gpt-tokenizer spells it for JavaScript, at commit
785c2695acbda31ae31ef8ab6343bcd7f1dde72f, release 4.1.2 (https://github.com/niieani/gpt-tokenizer).

